          "title": "You'll want to know: ಪ್ರಯಾಣ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪ್ರಯಾಣ (prayāṇa) — \"a journey\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit pra-yāṇa: pra, 'forth, forward', laid on a root meaning to go. A going-forth."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That pra- is very old and very widely travelled. It is the pro- of Latin, the pro- of Greek and the forth of English, one prefix that four languages inherited rather than borrowed from one another. Wish someone ಶುಭ ಪ್ರಯಾಣ (prayāṇa), a good journey, and half the phrase is a word this book taught you on a quite different errand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three: now, the day after tomorrow, a journey."
            }
          ]
        },
